  <calibre:title_sort>Mystery of the Barranca, The</calibre:title_sort>
 </rdf:Description>

 <rdf:Description rdf:about=''
  xmlns:dc='http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/'>
  <dc:date>
   <rdf:Seq>
    <rdf:li>2026-10-20T16:58:49+00:00</rdf:li>
   </rdf:Seq>
  </dc:date>
  <dc:description>
   <rdf:Alt>
    <rdf:li xml:lang='x-default'>&lt;p&gt;William Thornton and Robert Seyd are two American friends who share an interest in mining. They make an agreement that whoever finds a good prospect has to contact the other so that they can work together to exploit the mine. The day to honor this pact finally comes when Robert finds a rich copper mine in Guerrero, Mexico.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;On the way to the mine, William is struck by the beauty of an elegant young woman, accompanied by a large Siberian wolfhound, at a local train station. As the train approaches, the dog leaps onto the tracks. Robert, acting quickly, gets the dog to safety in the nick of time. The girlâ€™s companionâ€”the nephew of the general who owns the land under the mineâ€”offers the American duo men and mules to transport their equipment to their destination.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;What appears to be a stroke of good luck ends up becoming a prelude to a seemingly endless wave of challenges, as the bad omens surrounding the mine, and the generalâ€™s animosity towards Americans, threaten to lead William and Robert down a path of treachery and darkness.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
   </rdf:Alt>
  </dc:description>
  <dc:language>
   <rdf:Bag>
    <rdf:li>en</rdf:li>
   </rdf:Bag>
  </dc:language>
  <dc:publisher>
   <rdf:Bag>
    <rdf:li>Standard Ebooks</rdf:li>
   </rdf:Bag>
  </dc:publisher>
  <dc:subject>
   <rdf:Bag>
